  "header": {
    "subsystemType": "Hrot.Scenario",
    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "terrainName": "basic-desert",
    "description": "What: a flame sets a TIMBER building alight, never a brick one (CE-3488 flame FL-4, F-3; docs/designs/weapons/DESIGN_Flame_Weapons.md \u00a77c). On basic-desert the scenario places a 'Timber House' (the timber-house template: timber walls, 8 x 6 m, its SW corner at (300, 300)) and a 'Brick Shed' (the shed template, brick, at (300, 330)). 'Hut Man' stands in the timber house's far corner, out of the jet's cone; 'Shed Man' stands inside the shed. Two FlamethrowerSoldiers (friend) 15 m west each flame a solid stretch of their building's west wall (FireAtPoint, mount 0, 60 fuel shots). Judge: both spend fuel; after 2 s of flame the timber house is set alight and the man inside burns (the building's fire, not the jet) and dies; the brick shed never burns and its man is never hurt."
  },
